  "positioning": {
    "thesisLine": "Downtown Lowell landmark block at 26.52% below-market rents — $481,644 of marked GPR upside lifts the cap from 5.44% to 8.16%.",
    "strengths": [
      "53 units — 47 apartments over 6 ground-floor commercial spaces, 58,884 rentable SF (66,764 SF GBA), built 1906, converted 2016",
      "In-place rents 26.52% below market: $481,644/yr Below Market Rent line in the workbook; GSR $1,334,220 vs $1,815,864 GPR",
      "Cap rates: 5.86% T12 / 5.44% current / 8.16% pro forma at the $15,000,000 ask ($283,019/unit, $225/SF on GBA)",
      "Workbook debt model: 2.53% rate, 30-yr am, 75% LTV ($11,250,000 loan), $535,521 ADS, 1.52x DSCR, 7.47% current / 18.36% pro forma cash-on-cash",
      "High Achieved rents already prove the marks: $1,960 1BR / $2,200 2BR achieved in-building vs $1,890 / $2,050 current averages",
      "49 of 53 units occupied (92.5%); vacant: units 301, 402, 501 and former Dunkin Donuts space (COM2)"
    ],
    "marketNotes": [
      "CoStar (Jul 2026): Downtown Lowell submarket; subject asking $1,914/unit avg vs $2,234 submarket 3-5 star and $3,011 Boston market overall",
      "CoStar: submarket 3-5 star vacancy 4.8%; market sales price per unit $245,320 (12-mo)",
      "CoStar: subject in a federal Opportunity Zone; pedestrian rating 100 — exceptionally friendly",
